{id, source, claim, measure{script, corpus, n, gate, value, unit, worse}, status, killed_by, revive_if, note}

‼️ `value` / `unit` / `worse` must be COMPARABLE SCALARS. Statistics stuffed into a free-form dict cannot be diffed, and the interface degrades back into a transcribed table. `worse: "up"` says which direction is bad, without which a diff has no sign.

‼️ `measure.script` is the core of this interface, not decoration: next round re-measures with the SAME ruler rather than reporting an impression. `measure.corpus` is recorded for the same reason a run records its dataset identity — change the frame selection and you will read a rendering change as a model change.
